    },
    {
      "id": "window-glass",
      "origin": "Rendered from the original canonical glass cuts: three indigo panes and the amber lamp pane. The public-only soft lead finish gently reduces metal contrast and cement shadow; geometry, came widths, glass colours and the canonical logo are unchanged. Other painter callers retain the original finish.",
      "privacy": "Decorative illustration only."
    },
    {
      "id": "living-world",
      "origin": "Kept, a FellowSoft-authored score and rendered excerpt from the enhanced Stub music language.",
      "privacy": "No resident household records. Audio is visitor initiated."
    },
    {
      "id": "responsive-garden",
      "origin": "400px and 800px proportional derivatives of the reviewed invented North Hollow Garden photographs.",
      "privacy": "The original composition and demonstration records are unchanged.",
      "transform": "Resize only; original 1600px photographs remain available."
    },
    {
      "id": "film",
      "origin": "A Day to Keep, the FellowSoft-authored 48 second film of October 14, 2026: the marsh, the Window and Stub, drawn and scored in code. Web copies at 1080p and 720p; the poster and English captions are the cut's own.",
      "privacy": "Illustration, music and on-screen words only. No person, household, place record or voice is shown or heard.",
      "transform": "H.264 re-encodes of the reviewed master at constant quality 23 with fast start; the sound is copied unchanged; metadata removed."
    },
    {
      "id": "stub-folds-north-hollow",
      "origin": "A software capture, made October 17, 2026 in headless Chromium, of the front of North Hollow, the sealed FellowSoft Home demonstration this site carries at /home/demo/. Shown in North Hollow's window on Stub's paper until the live demonstration has loaded.",
      "privacy": "Invented household; no resident records. Its sky and weather are the demonstration's own.",
      "transform": "Captured at 1200 by 600 CSS pixels at 1.5x, resized to 1600 by 800 and encoded as WebP at quality 80; no retouching, no metadata."
    },
    {
      "id": "stub-folds-listening",
      "origin": "Out the Window, FellowSoft's weather album of October 14, 2026: thirteen pieces synthesized in code on the house score engine (the instruments and room of the film A Day to Keep), its album.json and its cover, carried byte for byte.",
      "privacy": "Music only. No voice, no sample, no recording and no model. Nothing is requested until the Listening fold is opened, and no piece plays until it is pressed.",
      "transform": "None. AAC at 128 kb/s, 48 kHz stereo, each piece at -16 LUFS integrated."
    },
    {
      "id": "stub-folds-marsh",
      "origin": "The house's own Finger Lakes marsh painter (finger-lakes.js and reading-adapter.mjs), as the FellowSoft television bundles it for Chrome 120, carried byte for byte. It draws the marsh in the visitor's browser from the site's own sky for the chosen hour.",
      "privacy": "Code only. It reads no clock, location, storage or network of its own; it is imported only when the living marsh is opened.",
      "transform": "None."
    },
    {
      "id": "stub-folds-plants",
      "origin": "Twenty-four of FellowSoft Home's botanical stamps from its first reviewed collection of October 11, 2026, at 512 and 128 pixels, with a catalogue of their names, family, habit and note written from the house's species library (scripts/build-stub-folds-media.mjs). The stamps are original illustrations made for the house with an image-generation model from each plant's own record and the house's stamp brief; botanical references informed anatomy only and no photograph was traced or incorporated.",
      "privacy": "Botanical illustration and plant facts only. The library's safety fields, which are not yet reviewed, are not carried.",
      "transform": "Stamps unchanged. The catalogue keeps a variety's apostrophe where the record keeps one among its other names, and capitalizes each note's first word."
    }
  ],
  "type": {
    "delivery": "Five same-origin font files. The two front faces also travel embedded in the document head so their first use cannot reset the text. No font service is contacted.",
    "notices": "/licenses/",
    "source": "Official Fontsource 5.3.0 packages; Latin WOFF2 members copied unchanged."
  },
  "browserState": {
    "intro": "One session-only flag remembers whether the arrival animation has played. It contains no identity or visit log.",
    "specimen": "The public compiler and curated PlainLedger runtime operate in memory. The specimen calls no model, network or persistent storage. Reloading clears its visitor-entered rows. A downloaded tool includes the rows the visitor chooses to keep. A Loom Card carries only the design; its recovered tool starts with empty rows.",
    "recipe": "The public Kitchen Rolodex holds selections, quantity factors and cooking progress per recipe in memory for this visit; the visitor may download a text copy. No model or private record book is contacted.",
    "film": "A Day to Keep is requested from this site only after a visitor presses Stub. It plays in the page and nothing about the viewing is kept.",
    "stubFolds": "Stub's folds keep nothing between visits: which page is open, the album's place and the marsh's hour live in memory and are gone when his paper closes."
  },
